# Frontend UI & Quality

## Component design

- Single responsibility; predictable props; minimal side effects.
- Prefer small composable components over god components.
- Extract reusable logic into hooks; keep UI components presentational.
- Avoid deep prop drilling — compose or use context/hooks deliberately.

## Tailwind

- Consistent spacing and typography; semantic tokens via theme when configured.
- Use `cn()` (clsx + tailwind-merge) for conditional classes.
- Avoid unreadable utility chains; extract repeated patterns to components or `@apply` sparingly.

## UX

- Handle loading, empty, and error states for every async UI.
- Responsive layouts; clear hierarchy; purposeful motion only.
- Never expose raw API errors or stack traces to users.

## Performance

- Prefer RSC and code splitting; lazy-load heavy client bundles.
- Memoize only when measured or clearly justified.
- Watch bundle size, render frequency, and expensive computations.

## API in the UI layer

- No `fetch` in presentational components — use `services/` and `hooks/`.
- Components consume hooks; hooks consume services.

## Anti-patterns

- Giant pages with all logic inline.
- Duplicated fetch calls across siblings.
- Global state for data that belongs on the server or in the URL.
- Chaotic one-off styling without shared patterns.
